      "id": "cfzma9c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is a mechanical longitudinal wave that requires a material medium to propagate and cannot travel through a vacuum.",
        "The characteristics of sound waves include amplitude (which determines loudness) and frequency (which determines pitch).",
        "Sound is classified into Infrasonic (<20 Hz), Audible (20 Hz - 20 kHz), and Ultrasonic (>20 kHz) waves based on frequency.",
        "An echo is formed by the reflection of sound and requires a minimum reflecting distance of 17.2 meters and a time lag of 0.1 seconds.",
        "Ultrasound applications include SONAR underwater distance measurement, medical echocardiography, and flaw detection in metals."
      ],
      "id": "jjchf8w"
    },
