    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Speed of sound is maximum in solids, lower in liquids, lowest in gases, and zero in a vacuum.",
        "The persistence of human hearing is 0.1 seconds, which determines the 17.2-meter minimum distance requirement for hearing a distinct echo.",
        "Pitch depends directly on the frequency of sound, whereas loudness depends on the square of the amplitude.",
        "SONAR employs ultrasonic waves to determine the depth of sea beds and detect underwater objects."
      ],
      "id": "qwbfd3m"
